[00:06.48] I got sunshine in my stomach
[00:13.04] Like I just rocked my baby to sleep
[00:19.91] I got sunshine in my stomach
[00:26.67] But I can't keep me from creeping sleep
[00:33.42] Sleep, deep in the deep
[01:18.62] Rockface moves to press my skin
[01:21.44] White liquids turn sour within
[01:23.86] Turn fast-turn sour
[01:26.47] Turn sweat-turn sour
[01:29.09] Must tell myself that I'm not here
[01:32.28] I'm drowning in a liquid fear
[01:35.02] Bottled in a strong compression
[01:37.62] My distortion shows obsession
[01:41.28] In the cave
[01:44.28] Get me out of this cave!
[01:51.10] If I keep my self-control
[01:53.60] I'll be safe in my soul
[01:55.96] And the childhood belief
[01:58.83] Brings a moment's relief
[02:01.76] But my cynic soon returns
[02:03.82] And the lifeboat burns
[02:07.65] My spirit just never learns
[02:14.65] Stalactites, stalagmites
[02:17.29] Shut me in, lock me tight
[02:19.87] Lips are dry, throat is dry
[02:22.56] Feel like burning, stomach churning
[02:25.27] I'm dressed up in a white costume
[02:27.96] Padding out leftover room
[02:30.62] Body stretching, feel the wretching
[02:35.31] In the cage
[02:39.35] Get me out of this cage!
[02:46.84] In the glare of a light
[02:49.28] I see a strange kind of sight
[02:51.75] Of cages joined to form a star
[02:54.79] Each person can't go very far
[02:57.52] All tied to their things
[03:00.08] They are netted by their strings
[03:02.73] Free to flutter in memories of their wasted wings
[03:09.94] 
[04:36.38] Outside the cage I see my Brother John
[04:42.05] He turns his head so slowly round
[04:46.03] I cry out help! before he can be gone
[04:53.08] And he looks at me without a sound
[05:03.28] And I shout 'John please help me!'
[05:05.75] But he does not even want to try to speak
[05:09.56] I'm helpless in my violent rage
[05:13.56] And a silent tear of blood dribbles down his cheek
[05:17.85] And I watch him turn away and leave the cage
[05:21.56] My little runaway
[05:24.87] 
[05:51.42] In a trap, feel a strap
[05:53.99] Holding still. Pinned for kill
[05:56.33] Chances narrow that I'll make it
[05:59.25] In the cushioned straight-jacket
[06:01.54] Just like 22nd Street
[06:04.28] When they got me by my neck and feet
[06:06.93] Pressures building, can't take any more
[06:09.32] My headaches charge. My earaches roar
[06:12.54] In the pain
[06:15.80] Get me out of this pain
[06:22.58] If I could change to liquid
[06:24.97] I could fill the cracks up in the rock
[06:28.02] But I know that I am solid
[06:29.63] And I am my own bad luck
[06:32.52] But outside John disappears and my cage dissolves
[06:37.81] Without any reason my body revolves
[06:46.89] Keep on turning
[06:49.01] Keep on turning
[06:51.73] Keep on turning
[06:54.37] Keep on turning
[06:56.95] Keep on turning
[06:58.92] Turning around
[07:03.72] Just spinning around
[07:11.58] 